From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:30:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.networking.sockets, windows.system.profile: two
 classes Office asks for.

MessageWebSocket is the second of the two the React Native workaround in
scripts/disable-office-reactnative.sh was written for; HttpBaseProtocolFilter,
the first, went in earlier.  With both here that workaround has nothing left to
work around.

The transport is winhttp, which already speaks the protocol: the upgrade
handshake, the framing, the close.  What this adds is the WinRT shape around it
-- the request headers gathered before connecting and sent with the handshake,
the control object, the two events -- and a receive thread that turns frames
back into MessageReceived, honouring both receive modes, and raises Closed with
the code and reason the peer sent rather than letting the socket go quiet.

MessageWebSocketControl is a settings object and is implemented outright.
Reaching a message's bytes is not: both ways of doing so return a
Windows.Storage.Streams type this tree does not have -- DataReader has no
implementation and no IDL, and there is no input stream over a buffer -- so
those two say exactly which class is missing rather than inventing a private
one here.  The event still fires, so a caller learns what arrived.

RetailInfo describes a retail demo device.  This is not one and cannot become
one, so demo mode is off and its property bag is empty, which is the answer
Windows gives on every machine that was not put into demo mode.  The empty bag
is a PropertySet's view: the collection in wintypes is already written and
already tested, and a second one here would only be a second thing to get
wrong.

Every IID is from the published metadata and was checked against Office's own
binaries, on the 16.0.20326 build this prefix actually runs -- the interface
set there is identical to the older one these were first read from.

tools/winrtprobe covers both: the socket activates, every interface each class
promises is reachable, the control's properties round-trip and refuse invalid
values, a request header is accepted and an empty name refused, and RetailInfo
answers for a machine that is not a demo unit.  24 of 24 checks pass against
the prefix Office runs in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 62af2f69e9a12df4d8d9f3ca89ebf080927d65a8)

