+/*
+ * The two event argument objects.
+ *
+ * WebSocketClosedEventArgs carries the close frame and is complete.
+ *
+ * MessageWebSocketMessageReceivedEventArgs says what arrived -- the type, and
+ * whether the message is whole -- and that much is complete too.  Reaching the
+ * bytes is not: both ways of doing so hand back a Windows.Storage.Streams type
+ * that Wine does not have.  DataReader has no implementation anywhere in the
+ * tree and no IDL either, and there is no input stream over a buffer to return
+ * instead.  Rather than invent a private one here, where nothing else could
+ * use it, these say exactly which class is missing.  The event still fires, so
+ * a caller learns a message arrived and what kind it was.
